                <pb facs="0117" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G/277: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-15T10:00:00-04:00">October 15, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. Referring further to Department’s telegram No. 76, October 10, 7 p.m., in
                    informal conversation with Undersecretary of Foreign Affairs last night he said
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Prensa</hi> editorial did not reflect views of his
                    Government. That as regards the Montevideo Conference, Argentina was “at the
                    orders” of the Uruguayan Government and that in his opinion it was now too late
                    to think of postponement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
